497	    /// The conversation. Lines use Yarn's "Speaker: text" form (DialogueSystem splits the
498	    /// speaker off). `<<emote who kind>>` drives the in-box portrait (left = NPC, right =
499	    /// player); `<<react who mark>>` pops an above-head reaction mark. Both arrive as a
500	    /// DialogueCommandMessage. The start node must be named "Start" (see NpcInteractionSystem).
501	    private const string YarnSource = @"title: Start
502	---
503	<<emote npc happy>>
504	Cow: Moo! A visitor! We don't get many folks wandering out to my little meadow.
505	Cow: What brings you all the way out here, friend?
506	<<emote player question>>
507	-> I'm just exploring the area.
508	    <<emote npc happy>>
509	    Cow: Exploring! Wonderful. There's no finer patch of grass this side of the river.
510	    <<emote player happy>>
511	    <<react player star>>
512	    Player: It really is peaceful out here.
513	-> Do you ever get lonely?
514	    <<emote npc sad>>
515	    Cow: ...Sometimes. The days are long and the field is wide.
516	    <<emote npc happy>>
517	    <<react npc star>>
518	    Cow: But a good chat like this one? That keeps me going.
519	-> Wait, can cows really talk?
520	    <<emote player surprised>>
521	    <<react player question>>
522	    Player: Wait... can cows actually talk?
523	    <<emote npc surprised>>
524	    <<react npc exclaim>>
525	    Cow: Can't yours?
526	    <<emote player surprised>>
527	    Player: ...Fair enough.
528	<<emote npc happy>>
529	Cow: Do come visit again. The meadow's always right here.
530	<<react npc star>>
531	===
532	";
